# Flash-attention backward, main kernel: one CTA per key block walks
# the query blocks at or after it, 160 bf16 mma per iteration (five
# 64x64x128 GEMMs over 8 warps). The trip count is the number of query
# blocks at or after the CTA's, one value per CTA. Over the record's
# 32x12 CTAs its sum, Σ (32 − x) · 12 = 6336 trips, gives 259,522,560
# mma per launch, and the loop's executions agree with the RTX 4090's.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/attn_bwd_kernel.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/gluon/attn_bwd_kernel.sm_89.ptx --ncu %fixtures/gluon/attn_bwd_kernel.sm_89.ncu.json | FileCheck --check-prefix=REC "%s"
CHECK: kernel attn_bwd_kernel
CHECK: block size: 256 threads, 8 warps (256x1x1 from .reqntid)
CHECK: loop gluon_attn_bwd.py:112 ($L__BB0_2)
CHECK: trips = param_13 / 64 - %ctaid.x
CHECK: mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k16.row.col.f32.bf16.bf16.f32    160
CHECK: tensor flops = 20480  (bf16 20480)
# The `red` under `mov.pred %p20, -1` runs on every thread: its store is exact.
CHECK: global bytes: load <= 192 B, store 128 B
CHECK: unknowns:
CHECK: coverage: instructions_classified 100.0% (1247/1247)
REC: totals per launch [static]:
REC: tensor bf16{{ +}}259522560{{ +}}8110080{{$}}
REC: $L__BB0_2{{ +}}confirmed
